#!/usr/bin/env bash
# Every function's description and grants, in one place. Regenerates
# functions/<name>/<name>.json; never edit those by hand (bin/fnjson.py, as Tasks').
#   table   read        table:rw  + write rows        table:rwd  + delete rows
#   function:<name>     run it    workflow:<name>  start it    /folder:verbs   a folder
#   connector:<slug>    use the Lemma's connection
set -euo pipefail
cd "$(dirname "$0")/.."
f() { uv run --no-project python bin/fnjson.py "$@"; }
f prr_intake "A GitHub event or the sync to pull_request rows: risk from the team's risky paths and the size (lockfiles not counted), who wrote it, the issues it closes, and a review round queued when one is due (prr-review). event pull_request, pull_request_review, check_suite (settles pull requests at that commit), sync (a repository's open pull requests) or app (queue yes: Review again). No model." repository pull_request:rw prr_round:rw prr_settings prr_member prr_risk_path prr_merge_log:rw workflow:prr-review function:prr_settle connector:github
f prr_begin_round "Claim one queued review round and gather what code knows for the reviewer: the rules in scope, earlier findings and what people decided, the lines this push touched since the last round, and conflicts with other open pull requests. Posts the Lemma check as in progress, as the bot, when it is on." prr_round:rw pull_request:rw prr_rule prr_finding prr_settings:rw repository connector:github
f prr_save_round "Keep a review round: checks the reviewer's answer, matches findings by fingerprint across pushes (dismissed stays dismissed, gone on changed lines is fixed, nothing new on untouched lines), writes the ledger of every rule in scope, and the verdict code decides." prr_round:rw pull_request:rw prr_finding:rw prr_rule
f prr_settle "Where a pull request stands, by code: the verdict, who it waits on and for what, and whether it merges by itself (watch or merge). As the Lemma's bot only, when Settings say so: the Lemma check, the approval of a clean round and its withdrawal, the summary comment or the round's findings as a review." pull_request:rw prr_round:rw prr_finding:rw prr_rule prr_member prr_settings:rw repository prr_merge_log:rw connector:github
f prr_merge "Merge one pull request. mode due: every condition checked again at merge time, then GitHub's auto-merge, the merge queue or a squash, as the Lemma's bot (never as a person). mode person: the person's own one-press merge on their own GitHub (github-personal), once no rule is broken. Logged in prr_merge_log." pull_request:rw prr_round prr_finding prr_settings:rw repository prr_merge_log:rw function:prr_settle connector:github connector:github-personal
f prr_sync "Every 15 minutes: each watched repository's open pull requests through prr_intake, rounds that never finished failed, pull requests whose wait has passed merged through prr_merge, and clean ones still waiting on checks settled again." repository pull_request:rw prr_round:rw prr_settings function:prr_intake function:prr_settle function:prr_merge
f prr_send_back "Send a pull request back on GitHub as the Lemma's bot: one review requesting changes, with the open findings on their lines and the rule each breaks. Only when the bot posts; sending back as yourself is the app's." pull_request prr_round prr_finding:rw prr_rule prr_settings:rw function:prr_settle connector:github
f prr_fix_task "Fix it: a finding becomes a team task (source pr-review, the finding quoted, the pull request linked). assign_to none (default), coding_agent, me, or person with user_id. One task per finding." prr_finding:rw pull_request prr_rule task:rw
f prr_hold "Hold a pull request that is merging by itself (hold true), or let it go (hold false): it merges only if every condition still holds. Logged." pull_request:rw prr_merge_log:rw function:prr_settle
f prr_decide_finding "A person's call on a finding: not_worth_fixing (dismissed, never raised again), wrong (never raised again, counted against its rule) or reopen; then the pull request is settled again." prr_finding:rw function:prr_settle
f prr_read_rules "Read a repository's rule files at its default branch (AGENTS.md, CLAUDE.md, REVIEW.md, CONTRIBUTING.md, .github/copilot-instructions.md, .github/instructions/*.instructions.md, .cursor/BUGBOT.md) with numbered lines and what each applies to, and the review comments on its last 60 merged pull requests, for the scout. Without repo: starts prr-setup for each watched repository (Read the repositories again)." prr_rule repository workflow:prr-setup connector:github
f prr_save_rules "Keep the rules the scout proposed, checked by code: a rule from a file must quote it (its source becomes file:line where code found the words), one from review comments must quote two pull requests' comments word for word. Everything enters proposed unless set-up accepted the file rules." prr_rule:rw prr_settings
f prr_setup_save "PR review's set-up and Settings: repositories (review and merge mode, what GitHub says about each), who posts, the Lemma check, comments, approving, the merge conditions, the team's logins and risky paths. read_rules starts prr-setup per repository. Returns the schedules the app makes. Safe to run again." repository:rw prr_settings:rw prr_member:rw prr_risk_path:rw workflow:prr-setup connector:github
f prr_memory "Tells this Lemma's agents that PR review is installed: its block in /memory/AGENTS.md and its guide at /memory/plugins/pr-review.md, leaving the team's notes alone. Set-up runs it; safe to run again. remove takes both out." /memory:read,write
f prr_needs_you "What in PR review needs the person, written to the shared needs_you list (Today reads it): decide Review this (a pull request waiting on their review) and Merge this (a clean one ready for them to merge). Runs as the person; resolves what no longer applies." pull_request prr_round needs_you:rw
f prr_sample_data "load: a made-up team's acme/api and acme/web (ravi, mei, tom and you as asha) with ten open pull requests across the inbox, rules, findings over two pushes and a week of merging by itself. clear: removes only what the sample made and closes its Today items." repository:rwd pull_request:rwd prr_round:rwd prr_finding:rwd prr_rule:rwd prr_risk_path:rwd prr_member:rwd prr_settings:rwd prr_merge_log:rwd task:rwd needs_you:rw function:prr_needs_you
